BT /F2 12.00 Tf 1 0 0 1 62.00 767.89 Tm (7. Object-Oriented Design) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 62.00 748.89 Tm (The program is divided into layers. Model classes \(Student, Scholarship, SessionToken\) hold the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 62.00 733.89 Tm (data and are mapped to database tables. Repository interfaces read and write those models. Service) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 62.00 718.89 Tm (classes \(AuthService, ProfileService, MatchingService, RenewalService\) hold the business logic.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 62.00 703.89 Tm (Controllers expose the REST endpoints. The matching module uses an interface, EligibilityRule,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 62.00 688.89 Tm (implemented by one class per criterion, so a new rule can be added without changing the matching) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 62.00 673.89 Tm (service. The diagram in UML-Diagram.png shows these classes and their relationships.) Tj ET
